A shape written inside an `if` in a canvas body reaches every target's draw
function.

`passCanvas` keeps the conditionals and loops a canvas body was written with,
so a draw body is not a flat list of primitive calls. bubbletea's draw-func
walk read only the top level and appended an `ir.If` whole, which left the
calls inside it untranslated -- and because they name intrinsics no Go emitter
implements, the build did not emit bad code, it panicked:

    codegen: go has no implementation of intrinsic "CanvasSave"

So this fixture is a golden rather than a script test: the assertion is the
shape of the emitted draw function, per target, with the conditional intact
around translated calls.

Both shapes now draw from their target's own override, which is what #213
finished: the html output is the override's own statements, `cssColor` folds to
a string at build time, and `ctx.stroke()` is absent because
`style.stroke.a > 0` folded to false -- where the name-matched translation this
replaced emitted an invisible stroke on every fill-only shape (#225).

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `\b(CanvasSave|CanvasDraw|CanvasApplyStyle)\(` -- an untranslated canvas intrinsic names a Go function nobody emits; \b keeps the runtime helper _snglCanvasDraw out of it
deny out/none/html/index.html `\b(CanvasSave|CanvasDraw|CanvasApplyStyle)\(` -- same, for the JS translation

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import draw "sngl:ui/draw"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
}

component main() ui.node {
    var big = true

    draw.canvas(width=40px, height=20px) {
        if big {
            draw.rect(x=0.0, y=0.0, w=10.0, h=5.0, style=draw.CanvasStyle{fill=color{r=255}})
        } else {
            draw.circle(cx=5.0, cy=5.0, r=2.0, style=draw.CanvasStyle{fill=color{b=255}})
        }
    }
}

ui.window {
    main()
}
-- out/go/bubbletea/model.go --
